{"embedding_dim": 1536, "data": [{"__id__": "chunk-b863a770e3e09f63a61ec948466e1eee", "__created_at__": 1756570027, "content": "{\"feature\": \"Jellybean (Feature name for internal parental control system)-based parental notifications\", \"feature_description\": \"Parental notifications for minor access attempts to restricted features, using behavioral anomaly detection (IMT (Internal monitoring trigger) vs BB (Baseline Behavior; standard user behavior used for anomaly detection) models) and ShadowMode (Deploy feature in non-user-impact way to collect analytics only) enforcement with compliance logging (CDS (Compliance Detection System)) and geo-flags (Glow (A compliance-flagging status, internally used to indicate geo-based alerts))\", \"needs_geo_specific_logic\": true, \"reasoning\": \"Florida law requires age verification for access to material harmful to minors (Section 501.1737) and addresses addictive features including push notifications (Section 501.1736). The feature uses algorithmic analysis and dispatches notifications, falling within regulated behaviors. Geo-specific logic is needed to implement Florida's age verification requirements (both anonymous and standard methods), constrain notification behavior to avoid classification as addictive features, and ensure compliance with referenced Section 501.1738. However, the provided excerpts lack full text of Sections 501.1736 and 501.1738, creating uncertainty around explicit parental notification mandates and technical requirements.\", \"regions_affected\": {\"region\": \"Florida, US\", \"requirement_summary\": \"Implement age verification flows offering both anonymous and standard methods; treat parental notifications as potentially regulated push notifications and constrain them (target only verified parents, limit frequency); ensure compliance with Section 501.1738; provide parental control mechanisms and audit logging\", \"regulations\": [{\"name\": \"Florida Age Verification for Material Harmful to Minors\", \"citation\": \"Section 501.1737, Florida Statutes\", \"snippet\": \"must use either anonymous age verification or standard age verification to verify that the age of a person attempting to access the material is 18 years of age or older and prevent access to the material by a person younger than 18 years of age. The commercial entity must offer anonymous age verification and standard age verification\", \"source_id\": \"florida_state_law.txt\"}, {\"name\": \"Florida Social Media Use for Minors - Platform Characteristics\", \"citation\": \"Section 501.1736, Florida Statutes\", \"snippet\": \"Employs algorithms that analyze user data or information on users to select content for users; and ... b. Push notifications or alerts sent by the online forum, website, or application to inform a user about specific activities or events\", \"source_id\": \"florida_state_law.txt\"}, {\"name\": \"Reference to Section 501.1738 Requirements\", \"citation\": \"Section 501.1737, Florida Statutes\", \"snippet\": \"A commercial entity must ensure that the requirements of s. 501.1738 are met\", \"source_id\": \"florida_state_law.txt\"}]}, \"past_case_references\": [], \"confidence\": 0.6}", "full_doc_id": "doc-b863a770e3e09f63a61ec948466e1eee", "file_path": "unknown_source"}], "matrix": ""}